cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ProkName Studio in your research, please cite it as follows."
# Version (mirrors the engine's convention): the single source of truth
# is the `__version__` literal in src/prokname_studio/__init__.py, which pyproject.toml
# and the PyInstaller spec both read. CFF is plain YAML — it cannot execute that file —
# so the two `version:` fields below (this record and `preferred-citation`) are mirrors,
# kept honest by tests/test_citation_metadata.py, which fails if they drift.
title: "ProkName Studio: a bilingual, light/dark native desktop front-end for the ProkName prokaryotic nomenclature assistant"
authors:
  - family-names: "Zeng"
    given-names: "Zichao"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6553-970X"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-29"
license: MIT
license-url: "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZengZichao/ProkName-Studio"
keywords:
  - nomenclature
  - taxonomy
  - ICNP
  - SeqCode
  - LPSN
  - prokaryotes
  - desktop
  - gui
abstract: >-
  ProkName Studio is the native desktop front-end for prokname, a decision-support
  tool for prokaryotic nomenclature under the ICNP and the SeqCode. It exposes the
  engine's deterministic etymology-driven name generation, grammatical agreement
  validation, dual-code routing and two-tier deduplication through five panels, with
  a live Chinese / English interface switch and a light / dark appearance switch.
  Studio adds no naming logic of its own: every value on screen is returned by
  prokname's public API, and the engine is a dependency of this project rather than
  a layer inside it.
# The engine this front-end drives is a separate citable work; the version floor in
# pyproject.toml is the API contract these views were written against.
related-identifiers:
  - value: "ZengZichao/ProkName"
    type: repository
    relation: derives-from
